From 5063e8ecaef2206a1643f829a300989813a2fad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:10:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: build the strike army on time (the user:
 "if they were 4 units short, they need to fix their start")

The expert block's 5 strike-book games had 1-3 land units when the
build-up opened (T26-40) against plans of 8, and met the plan only at the
declaration (T63-83). Under EarlyStrike, before the strike (PREP,
BUILDUP), while the army is short of the plan's core or support count
(CvPlayer::IsEarlyStrikeArmyShort; empire-wide, in training included):
- the capital's fill-in is the army (GetEarlyStrikeArmyUnit: the core, or
  a unit that upgrades into it before the core's tech, e.g. a Warrior for
  a Spearman-class core, or the support), not CP's choice;
- the second city and the others train the army first, before their
  Monument and the normal AI;
- no building in any city unless it's in danger;
- no worker beyond one.
Both keep WarBudget's gold guard (GetAffordableWarUnits(10) >= 1). K stays
Personality's. On ai/war f9c16cd + patch 0037. Written 6:10am ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
